{"seq":47,"gate":"spec-lint","ticket":"T-01M2DND1F5N336Q3GKXGSXKWFP","data":{"verified":true},"files":{".adlc/specs/backlog-grooming.md":"ac2e80df564aba6228579f49b20e612226829ead162c4756716423bb16761d66"},"ts":"2026-09-13T15:15:43.611Z","prev":"8f5077473cba3b984e785695f5d51dd96c818db858e91ab55fa10b2d1c98ad8f","sig":"e3a3e7dab4dbf97884b581e012e605d5bdce459012fca0d67fb4857bbcc78511"}
{"seq":48,"gate":"premortem","ts":"2026-09-13T15:16:10.420Z","ticket":"T-01M2DND1F5N336Q3GKXGSXKWFP","data":{"promptOnly":true,"usageStatus":"unreported","verdict":"{\n  \"verdict\": \"analysed\",\n  \"causes\": [\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The mechanical check anchors on the cited LINE number, so any unrelated edit above the citation shifts the lines below it, the snippet no longer matches at that line, and a live bug is verdicted `fixed` and autonomously closed.\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.3: the line is a hint, never an identity; `fixed` requires the snippet to be absent from the WHOLE file. AC13 pins it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The one-shot review property is stated in SKILL.md prose, so a wrapper under pressure to finish re-runs the reviewer on a reworded artifact until it approves — the exact failure one-shot exists to prevent, and instructions do not stop it.\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.6: the core records the gate verdict against (issue, contentHash) and refuses a second attempt for the same revision. AC14.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The skill shells `gh issue close` directly, bypassing the floor, the gate and comment-first in one call — structurally the same gap as rails-guard's un-gated Bash surface.\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.6: every write flows through the core; a guard test asserts the shipped SKILL.md contains no mutating gh invocation. AC17.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"An issue with no parseable reference has no content-hash cache component, so its key degrades to updatedAt alone; code changes then never invalidate it and a `valid` verdict persists after the bug is fixed — reintroducing the decay the tool exists to detect, inside the tool's own cache.\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §4: such issues are re-verified every run, or cached only as `unverifiable` — never as `valid`. AC16.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"Comment-then-act is not atomic. A comment succeeds and the action fails (rate limit, revoked token, a human closing it first), leaving a `closing because…` comment on an open issue; every retry adds another comment.\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.8: durable marker per (issue, contentHash); a re-run detects its own marker and resumes at the action. AC15.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The autonomy floor lives in a repo file, so anyone who can land a PR can set it to [] and unlock autonomous closing — a one-line PR is the whole escalation path.\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.7: the profile is a trust root with rails-guard's asymmetry — narrowing is ordinary, widening is privileged. AC18. Human decision at P1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"Relations are O(n^2) — 370 issues is ~68,000 pairs. Exhaustive judgment is impractical; a cheap prefilter is similarity scoring, which the spec forbids as evidence.\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.4: similarity is a candidate FILTER, never evidence, and the filter's recall is the reported ceiling on findable relations. AC19. Human decision at P1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"On a repo where few issues carry parseable references, nearly everything routes to `model` (expensive) or `unverifiable` (no conclusion), and a sweep that examined almost nothing reads as thorough.\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.9: every run leads with its route distribution, the same honesty rule as `truncated`. AC20. Human decision at P1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"AC12 claimed the emitted set is consumable by issue-lanes while the spec explicitly does not modify issue-lanes, so the criterion tested a shape nobody consumes and later schema drift would break the handoff silently.\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.9: the set carries a schema version and AC12 pins it against a committed fixture; issue-lanes adoption is a separate ticket. Human decision at P1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"A mid-sweep gh rate limit or partial failure leaves some actions applied and some not, with the cache possibly written, and a re-run compounds rather than resumes.\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"status\": \"folded\",\n      \"resolution\": \"Spec §3.8: a mid-sweep failure must leave a resumable state, never a half-applied one; the marker makes resumption idempotent. AC15.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"unresolved\": 0\n}","specPath":".adlc/specs/backlog-grooming.md"},"files":{".adlc/specs/backlog-grooming.md":"ac2e80df564aba6228579f49b20e612226829ead162c4756716423bb16761d66"},"prev":"ad6abc79c3e11ff1f4dc39402ba30e2f1dd4648691879b4255a73205672e8dfc","sig":"e7b02539c58f881bcac83ad97e63878f0dc0fa352d0c55ce308d3c244048ab8f"}
{"seq":49,"gate":"spec-approval","ts":"2026-09-13T15:16:37.558Z","ticket":"T-01M2DND1F5N336Q3GKXGSXKWFP","data":{"approver":"Chris Williams","spec_hash":"ac2e80df564aba6228579f49b20e612226829ead162c4756716423bb16761d66","verdict":"approved","rounds":2,"questions":8,"sources":["parallax","premortem","interview-me"],"unresolved":0,"approved_assumptions":["The repo profile is JSON rather than markdown, deviating from .claude/release-profile.md, because it is parsed by code and must fail closed on malformed input","issue-lanes is not modified by this work; adopting the emitted set is a follow-on change with its own ticket"]},"files":{".adlc/specs/backlog-grooming.md":"ac2e80df564aba6228579f49b20e612226829ead162c4756716423bb16761d66"},"prev":"699b6a22731b57b0583da275b46e6082655419a166035bd72562a7682aa9b327","sig":"4c2fee91d36ea3a429a5b0db32bcb99b39a21c34fb91cd1c345031f94200f54d"}
